# Universe content · gas giants and ice giants
# researched: Wikipedia "Gas giant"; Universe Today "Gas Giants" (NASA-based); Sudarsky et al. 2000
#   "Albedo and Reflection Spectra of Extrasolar Giant Planets"
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r06-planet.md

# ── Kinds ──

@giant gas-giant
name: Gas giant
real: yes
makeup: mostly hydrogen and helium, a few percent heavier elements
example: Jupiter, Saturn
air: hydrogen 90%, helium 10%, methane 0.3%, ammonia 0.03%  (like Jupiter)

@giant ice-giant
name: Ice giant
real: yes
makeup: mostly water, ammonia and methane "ices" under a hydrogen-helium air
example: Uranus, Neptune
air: hydrogen 80%, helium 19%, methane 1.5%  (methane makes it blue, like Neptune)

@giant super-jupiter
name: Super-Jupiter
real: yes
says: heavier than Jupiter; above a point, extra mass makes it shrink instead of grow

@giant super-neptune
name: Super-Neptune
real: yes
says: between Neptune and Saturn in mass

@giant hot-jupiter
name: Hot Jupiter
real: yes
says: a gas giant in a tight, fast orbit close to its star, hot and puffed up
air: hydrogen 85%, helium 14%, water, carbon monoxide, sodium and potassium vapour  (scorching)

@giant hot-neptune
name: Hot Neptune
real: yes
says: an ice giant close to its star

@giant cold-jupiter
name: Cold Jupiter
real: yes
says: a gas giant far from its star, beyond about 1 au

@giant super-puff
name: Super-puff
real: yes
says: only a few Earths of mass, but wider than Neptune; as light as cotton candy

@giant eccentric-jupiter
name: Eccentric Jupiter
real: yes
says: a giant on a stretched orbit, swinging near and far

# ── Cloud classes (Sudarsky, by temperature) ──

@cloudclass sudarsky-1
name: Ammonia-cloud giant
real: yes
says: cold giants far out, with ammonia clouds, like Jupiter

@cloudclass sudarsky-2
name: Water-cloud giant
real: yes
says: warmer, with clouds of water

@cloudclass sudarsky-3
name: Cloudless giant
real: yes
says: too warm for clouds, a clear blue color

@cloudclass sudarsky-4
name: Alkali-metal giant
real: yes
says: hot, with sodium and potassium in the air, dark

@cloudclass sudarsky-5
name: Silicate-cloud giant
real: yes
says: hottest, with clouds of rock and iron

# ── Layers ──

# from-r, to-r: where the layer lies, as shares of the planet's radius from its middle (Jupiter: metallic hydrogen from
#   about 0.8 of the way out, a core of rock and metal in the inner 0.1 to 0.2, perhaps fuzzy); matter: what going in finds
#   there (air: its gases; plasma: hydrogen crushed into protons in a sea of free electrons; ice: hot dense water,
#   ammonia and methane; core: rock, iron and ice).
@layer cloud-tops
name: Cloud tops
from-r: 0.99
to-r: 1
matter: air
real: yes
says: layers of ammonia and water clouds at the top

@layer molecular-hydrogen
name: Molecular hydrogen layer
from-r: 0.8
to-r: 0.99
matter: air
real: yes
says: squeezed hydrogen gas, thickening into liquid with depth

@layer metallic-hydrogen
name: Metallic hydrogen layer
from-r: 0.15
to-r: 0.8
matter: plasma
real: yes
says: hydrogen crushed so hard it conducts electricity like metal; makes up most of a gas giant and drives its huge magnetic field
in: gas-giant, hot-jupiter

@layer ice-mantle
name: Ice mantle
from-r: 0.15
to-r: 0.85
matter: ice
real: yes
says: in ice giants, hot dense water, ammonia and methane under pressure
in: ice-giant

@layer core
name: Core
from-r: 0
to-r: 0.15
matter: core
real: yes
says: a likely core of rock and metal at the center

@layer helium-rain
name: Helium rain
real: yes
says: on Saturn, helium falls as droplets through the metallic hydrogen, heating the planet

# ── Features ──

@feature belts-and-zones
name: Belts and zones
real: yes
says: dark belts and light zones of cloud circling the planet, driven by fast winds and fast spin

@feature giant-storm
name: Giant storm
real: yes
says: a storm that can last centuries and be bigger than Earth
example: Jupiter's Great Red Spot

@feature rings
name: Rings
real: yes
says: ice and rock circling the planet in thin bands
example: Saturn's rings

@feature moon-system
name: Moon system
real: yes
says: giants gather many moons, from tiny rocks to worlds with their own air or hidden oceans

@feature magnetosphere
name: Giant magnetosphere
real: yes
says: a huge magnetic bubble; Jupiter's is among the largest structures in the Solar System

@feature auroras
name: Polar auroras
real: yes
says: bright auroras at both poles

# ── Solar System examples ──

@example jupiter
name: Jupiter
real: yes
type: gas-giant
note: the biggest planet, the Great Red Spot, dozens of moons

@example saturn
name: Saturn
real: yes
type: gas-giant
note: the great ring system, helium rain, dozens of moons

@example uranus
name: Uranus
real: yes
type: ice-giant
note: spins on its side

@example neptune
name: Neptune
real: yes
type: ice-giant
note: the farthest planet from the Sun, with the fastest winds

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule giant-seed
real: rule
says: every giant is generated live from the world seed; nothing is pre-built

@rule giant-zone
real: rule
says: giants form beyond the frost line; some wander inward to become hot Jupiters and hot Neptunes

@rule giant-clouds
real: rule
says: a giant's temperature picks its cloud class, from ammonia clouds when cold to rock clouds when hottest

@rule giant-layers
real: rule
says: gas giants get clouds, molecular hydrogen, metallic hydrogen and a core; ice giants get clouds, an ice mantle and a core

@rule giant-weather
real: rule
says: fast spin makes belts, zones and long-lived giant storms

@rule giant-moons-rings
real: rule
says: giants collect many moons and often rings; some moons can hold life

@rule giant-resources
real: rule
says: civilizations skim giants for hydrogen, helium-3 and deuterium fuel
